/// Bandit.HTTP2.StreamProcess: one process per stream, running the
/// pipeline. Spawned monitored by the connection when a stream's first
/// HEADERS arrives, and stops normally when done. The connection learns
/// of the end through the DOWN message and resets or forgets the stream
/// there — the stream process never waits on its own mailbox.
///
/// The process is a plain monitored process (`spawn_monitor`), not an
/// actor: spawning an actor makes the connection wait for the new
/// process's init, once per stream, in the connection's own loop
/// (BT-4469). Nothing calls a stream process, so it needs no mailbox
/// protocol. Its process dictionary carries `markerKey` so tools (the
/// stress tests' stream killer) can find stream processes.
///
/// An abnormal end (a leaked raise past the pipeline's own handling)
/// is swallowed here the way Bandit's handle_error returns normally:
/// the 500 already went out through sendOnError, and the connection
/// resets the stream on the DOWN message.
typed Object subclass: StreamProcess

  /// Spawn a monitored stream process running the pipeline on
  /// transport; answers {pid, monitorRef}. The monitor is the caller's
  /// (the connection's), set atomically with the spawn.
  class sealed spawnFor: transport :: HTTP2Stream handler: handler :: ExchangeHandlerLike config: config :: BuccaneerConfig connData: connData :: Tuple(Boolean, Tuple | Symbol) span: span :: CatalinaTelemetry | Nil -> Tuple =>
    Erlang erlang
      spawn_monitor: [
        StreamProcess
          run: transport
          handler: handler
          config: config
          connData: connData
          span: span
      ]

  /// The stream process body: mark the process, run the pipeline.
  class sealed run: transport :: HTTP2Stream handler: handler :: ExchangeHandlerLike config: config :: BuccaneerConfig connData: connData :: Tuple(Boolean, Tuple | Symbol) span: span :: CatalinaTelemetry | Nil -> Nil =>
    ProcessDictionary at: StreamProcess markerKey put: true
    [
      Pipeline
        runRequest: transport
        handler: handler
        connectionSpan: span
        connData: connData
        options: config
    ] on: Exception do: [:e :: Exception | nil]
    nil

  /// The process-dictionary key that marks a stream process.
  class sealed markerKey -> Symbol => #buccaneer_h2_stream
